{"title":"2011 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine the number of positive divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/c/29c67e73f7228e6d28145ab45b727ce951e9e21a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18~800$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"14\" /> that are divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/6/ec670a6cc74a8a120be9f280800052ca2600c563.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$235$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/c/b8c0545a1bda889d999488203a17da5278a157a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18~800 = 235 \\times 80 = 235 \\times 2^{4} \\times 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"266\" height=\"18\" />, meaning that for a number to be a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/c/29c67e73f7228e6d28145ab45b727ce951e9e21a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18~800$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"14\" /> but divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/6/ec670a6cc74a8a120be9f280800052ca2600c563.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$235$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, it must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/6/ec670a6cc74a8a120be9f280800052ca2600c563.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$235$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> times some power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> multiplied by either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Using this, we see that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/d/9edda2ccf704a82689f6bc631a75b007d0aec9c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\times 2 = \\boxed{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"96\" height=\"25\" /> divisors.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CSMC\" title=\"2011 CSMC\">2011 CSMC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CSMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CSMC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CSMC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CSMC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2011 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 3\">Part A Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Part A Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_1\" title=\"2011 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 1\">Part A 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2\" title=\"2011 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 2\">Part A 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2011 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 3\">Part A 3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Part A 4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Part A 5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Part A 6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1\" title=\"2011 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1\">Part B 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">Part B 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?titl